<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia Central Bank 1996 net profit fell sharply.</title>
<headline>Colombia Central Bank 1996 net profit fell sharply.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The net profit of Colombia's central bank fell to 138.14 billion pesos in 1996 from 294.24 billion in 1995, Finance Minister Jose Antonio Ocampo said.</p>
<p>He gave no reason for the sharp drop in profits, which the Banco de la Republica reaps largely from its handling of foreign reserves, but said the bank's total assets rose to 12.79 trillion pesos in 1996 from 11.08 trillion the previous year.</p>
<p>((-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
